@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@samp{wsp} is a WhatsApp client for Emacs: you read your chats@comma{} reply@comma{} react@comma{} edit@comma{} delete@comma{} send files@comma{} search and get notified@comma{} as on the phone.

@samp{wsp} has no WhatsApp connection of its own.  @uref{https://github.com/benthamite/wa-archive, wa-archive}@comma{} a daemon built on the whatsmeow library and linked to your phone as a companion device@comma{} holds the connection and keeps every message in an SQLite store.  @samp{wsp} reads that store directly@comma{} read-only@comma{} and does everything that acts on WhatsApp through wa-archive's local API@comma{} a Unix socket.  This is the arrangement sgn has with signal-cli: the daemon is the backend and @samp{wsp} the client.  Because the store holds the whole history@comma{} a chat shows as much of it as you load@comma{} and any message can be opened by its id@comma{} which lets other programs link to a message.

The parts:

@itemize
@item
reading: the chat list (@ref{The chat list, , The chat list})@comma{} chat buffers (@ref{Reading a chat, , Reading a chat}) and attachments (@ref{Attachments, , Attachments});
@item
writing: sending@comma{} replying@comma{} editing@comma{} deleting and reacting (@ref{Sending and acting on messages, , Sending and acting on messages});
@item
finding: search (@ref{Searching, , Searching}) and opening a chat at a given message (@ref{Opening a chat at a message, , Opening a chat at a message});
@item
staying current: read state@comma{} notifications and the unread indicator (@ref{Read state notifications and the indicator, , Read state@comma{} notifications and the indicator}).
@end itemize

@strong{Prerequisites}: Emacs 31.1 or later with SQLite support (@samp{wsp} opens the store with @code{sqlite-open}'s read-only argument@comma{} new in 31.1)@comma{} and @uref{https://github.com/benthamite/wa-archive, wa-archive} running and linked to your phone (its README explains how).  Without the daemon's socket@comma{} @samp{wsp} still shows the store but cannot act.

