@node Where wa-archive keeps its files
@section Where wa-archive keeps its files

@vindex wsp-data-directory
@vindex wsp-state-directory
@vindex wsp-api-socket
The user option @code{wsp-data-directory} is wa-archive's data directory@comma{} which holds the store @samp{messages.db}@comma{} the downloaded attachments under @samp{media/} and the API socket.  Its default is @samp{wa-archive} under @samp{$XDG_DATA_HOME}@comma{} or under @samp{~/.local/share} when that variable is unset@comma{} which is where wa-archive puts it.

The user option @code{wsp-state-directory} is wa-archive's state directory@comma{} which holds its heartbeat and the markers it leaves when unlinked or rejected as outdated (@ref{The daemon's health, , The daemon's health}).  Its default is @samp{wa-archive} under @samp{$XDG_STATE_HOME}@comma{} or under @samp{~/.local/state}.

The user option @code{wsp-api-socket} is the path of wa-archive's API socket.  The default@comma{} @code{nil}@comma{} means @samp{api.sock} in @code{wsp-data-directory}.  Change these only if wa-archive runs with other directories.

@node Connection and refresh
@section Connection and refresh

@vindex wsp-api-timeout
@vindex wsp-refresh-interval
@vindex wsp-heartbeat-max-age
The user option @code{wsp-api-timeout} is how many seconds @samp{wsp} waits for the daemon to answer a request; the default is @samp{30}.  A request left unanswered is treated as having an unknown outcome@comma{} never as failed (@ref{What happens when you send, , What happens when you send}).  Downloads wait up to 130 seconds regardless.

The user option @code{wsp-refresh-interval} is how many seconds pass between checks for changes the daemon did not announce@comma{} such as a finished download@comma{} a change in the daemon's health@comma{} or messages stored while @samp{wsp} was disconnected.  The default is @samp{3}.  New messages do not wait for it: the daemon announces them and they appear at once.

The user option @code{wsp-heartbeat-max-age} is the age in seconds after which wa-archive's heartbeat counts as stale; the default is @samp{3600}@comma{} the daemon's own monitoring threshold.

@node Chat display
@section Chat display

@vindex wsp-history-page-size
@vindex wsp-message-grouping-interval
@vindex wsp-prompt
The user option @code{wsp-history-page-size} is how many messages a chat buffer first shows@comma{} and how many more each @samp{C-c C-l} adds; the default is @samp{200}.

The user option @code{wsp-message-grouping-interval} is how many seconds may pass between a sender's messages for them to share one header; the default is @samp{300}.  A new day always starts a new header.

The user option @code{wsp-prompt} is the string before the input area; the default is @samp{"> "}.

@node Attachments (1)
@section Attachments

@vindex wsp-inline-images
@vindex wsp-image-max-width
@vindex wsp-auto-fetch-images
@vindex wsp-audio-players
The user option @code{wsp-inline-images}@comma{} @code{t} by default@comma{} shows downloaded images in the chat; @code{wsp-image-max-width} (default @samp{320}) caps their width in pixels.

The user option @code{wsp-auto-fetch-images}@comma{} @code{t} by default@comma{} has wa-archive download the images of a chat when the chat is drawn@comma{} as the phone does on Wi-Fi.  Each image is requested once per Emacs session.  Set it to @code{nil} to download images only when you press @samp{RET} on them.

The user option @code{wsp-audio-players} lists the programs tried@comma{} in order@comma{} to play voice notes and audio; the first found in the variable @code{exec-path} is used.  The default is @samp{("afplay" "mpv" "ffplay")}.

@node Read receipts typing and online status
@section Read receipts@comma{} typing and online status

@vindex wsp-mark-read
@vindex wsp-send-typing
@vindex wsp-send-presence
These options decide what your contacts see of your use of @samp{wsp}.

The user option @code{wsp-mark-read}@comma{} @code{t} by default@comma{} makes showing a chat mark its messages read@comma{} which sends read receipts: senders see blue ticks@comma{} as when you open the chat on the phone.  A chat counts as shown when its buffer is in the selected window of a frame that has focus; a terminal frame whose focus Emacs cannot tell never counts (@ref{Read state notifications and the indicator, , Read state@comma{} notifications and the indicator}).  Whether WhatsApp passes the receipts on also depends on your account's privacy setting.

The user option @code{wsp-send-typing}@comma{} @code{nil} by default@comma{} tells the chat when you are typing in its input area.

The user option @code{wsp-send-presence}@comma{} @code{nil} by default@comma{} shows you as online while Emacs has focus and a @samp{wsp} buffer is selected@comma{} and offline otherwise and when Emacs exits.  With both left off@comma{} @samp{wsp} sends no typing or presence at all.

@node Notifications and drafts
@section Notifications and drafts

@vindex wsp-notify
@vindex wsp-notify-show-text
@vindex wsp-drafts-file
@vindex wsp-reaction-choices
The user option @code{wsp-notify}@comma{} @code{t} by default@comma{} shows a desktop notification for incoming messages while @samp{wsp} runs.  The user option @code{wsp-notify-show-text}@comma{} @code{t} by default@comma{} puts the message text in the notification; set it to @code{nil} to show only who wrote.

The user option @code{wsp-drafts-file} is where input you have not sent is kept when you kill a chat buffer or exit Emacs@comma{} so it comes back when you open the chat again.  The default is @samp{wsp-drafts.eld} in your Emacs directory.  The file holds message text@comma{} so it is created readable only by you.  If the file cannot be read@comma{} @samp{wsp} leaves it alone rather than overwrite the other chats' drafts@comma{} and says so.

The user option @code{wsp-reaction-choices} lists the reactions @code{wsp-chat-react} offers first; you can also type any emoji.

@node Faces
@chapter Faces

@vindex wsp-header-face
@vindex wsp-own-header-face
@vindex wsp-timestamp-face
@vindex wsp-quote-face
@vindex wsp-deleted-face
@vindex wsp-annotation-face
@vindex wsp-read-face
@vindex wsp-media-face
@vindex wsp-system-face
@vindex wsp-reaction-face
@vindex wsp-pending-face
@vindex wsp-error-face
@vindex wsp-target-face
@vindex wsp-prompt-face
@vindex wsp-list-unread-face
@vindex wsp-list-count-face
In chat buffers@comma{} @code{wsp-header-face} and @code{wsp-own-header-face} show the headers above other people's messages and yours@comma{} and @code{wsp-timestamp-face} their times.  @code{wsp-quote-face} shows the quoted message of a reply and voice transcripts@comma{} @code{wsp-deleted-face} deleted messages@comma{} @code{wsp-annotation-face} marks such as @samp{(edited)} and the grey ticks@comma{} @code{wsp-read-face} the ticks of a message the recipient read@comma{} @code{wsp-media-face} attachment labels@comma{} @code{wsp-system-face} WhatsApp records that are not messages@comma{} and @code{wsp-reaction-face} reactions.  @code{wsp-pending-face} shows a message being sent and @code{wsp-error-face} one that may have been sent.  @code{wsp-target-face} highlights the message @code{wsp-open-message} opened at until your next command@comma{} and @code{wsp-prompt-face} is the prompt's face.

In the chat list@comma{} @code{wsp-list-unread-face} shows the names of chats with unread messages and @code{wsp-list-count-face} the unread counts; the latter also colours the mode-line indicator.

@node Variables and keymaps
@chapter Variables and keymaps

@vindex wsp-chat-mode-map
@vindex wsp-chat-message-map
@vindex wsp-list-mode-map
@vindex wsp-search-mode-map
@vindex wsp-chat-key
@vindex wsp-health-warning
@vindex wsp-api-event-functions
@vindex wsp-api-status-functions
@code{wsp-chat-mode-map} is active everywhere in a chat buffer; @code{wsp-chat-message-map} only on messages in the history@comma{} so its single-letter keys do not get in the way of typing.  @code{wsp-list-mode-map} and @code{wsp-search-mode-map} are the keymaps of the chat list and of search results.

In a chat buffer@comma{} @code{wsp-chat-key} holds the chat's canonical key.  @code{wsp-health-warning} holds the current warning about the daemon@comma{} or @code{nil} (@ref{The daemon's health, , The daemon's health}).

The hooks @code{wsp-api-event-functions} and @code{wsp-api-status-functions} run@comma{} respectively@comma{} with each event plist the daemon pushes and with no argument whenever the connection to it opens or closes.  @samp{wsp} uses them to redraw; you can add functions to react to events yourself.

