@node The chat list
@section The chat list

@findex wsp
@findex wsp-list-mode
@findex wsp-list-open
@samp{M-x wsp} opens the chat list@comma{} the buffer @samp{*wsp*} in @code{wsp-list-mode}@comma{} and connects to wa-archive if needed.  It lists every chat that has messages@comma{} most recent first@comma{} with the number of unread messages@comma{} the time of the latest message and a preview of it; in a group the preview names the sender.  A chat's name is the one wa-archive has for it; an unnamed direct chat takes the contact's latest display name@comma{} else the phone number.

@samp{RET} (@code{wsp-list-open}) opens the chat on the line@comma{} @samp{c} runs @code{wsp-chat}@comma{} @samp{s} runs @code{wsp-search} and @samp{g} redraws the list.  The list redraws itself as messages arrive.  When wa-archive is unlinked@comma{} outdated or silent@comma{} the header line says so instead of showing the column titles.

@findex wsp-chat
@samp{M-x wsp-chat} opens a chat chosen by name@comma{} including chats with no messages yet.  Names shared by several chats are told apart by number.  Typing a number with a leading @samp{+} that matches no name opens a chat with that number.

@findex wsp-stop
@samp{M-x wsp-stop} disconnects from wa-archive and stops redrawing; buffers stay but no longer change.  @samp{wsp} also stops by itself when you kill its last buffer.

@node Reading a chat
@section Reading a chat

@findex wsp-chat-mode
@findex wsp-chat-load-more
@findex wsp-chat-next-message
@findex wsp-chat-previous-message
A chat buffer@comma{} named @samp{*wsp: NAME*} and in @code{wsp-chat-mode}@comma{} has the history above and the prompt and input area below.  The history is read-only and drawn from the store; it redraws when the chat changes@comma{} keeping your input@comma{} its undo history@comma{} point and the start of every window showing it on the same message.

Messages are grouped under a header naming the sender and time.  Each shows the message it replies to (@samp{┃ Name: text})@comma{} its text with @samp{(edited)} if edited@comma{} @samp{[deleted]} if deleted@comma{} its attachment (@ref{Attachments, , Attachments}) and its reactions grouped by emoji.  Your own messages end in @samp{✓} once sent@comma{} grey @samp{✓✓} once delivered and coloured @samp{✓✓} once read.  WhatsApp records that are not messages@comma{} such as @samp{[messageHistoryNotice]}@comma{} are dimmed.

The buffer first shows the newest @code{wsp-history-page-size} messages.  @samp{C-c C-l} (@code{wsp-chat-load-more})@comma{} or @samp{g} on a message@comma{} adds as many older ones@comma{} back to the start of the archive.  Loaded history stays loaded as new messages arrive.  On messages@comma{} @samp{n} and @samp{p} move to the next and previous message.

The header line shows the chat's name@comma{} whether it is a group@comma{} the reply in progress (whom and what you are replying to) or the edit in progress@comma{} and any problem with the connection or the daemon.

@node Sending and acting on messages
@section Sending and acting on messages

@findex wsp-chat-return
@findex wsp-chat-send-input
@findex wsp-chat-cancel
Type in the input area and press @samp{RET} (@code{wsp-chat-return}) to send; @samp{S-RET} or @samp{C-j} inserts a newline.  On the history@comma{} @samp{RET} opens what is at point instead (@ref{Attachments, , Attachments}).  @code{wsp-chat-send-input} sends the input as a reply or an edit when one is in progress; @samp{C-c C-k} (@code{wsp-chat-cancel}) cancels that.

@findex wsp-chat-reply
@findex wsp-chat-edit
@findex wsp-chat-delete
@findex wsp-chat-react
@findex wsp-chat-copy
On a message:

@itemize
@item
@samp{r} (@code{wsp-chat-reply}) makes the next message a reply to it;
@item
@samp{e} (@code{wsp-chat-edit}) puts one of your messages in the input to edit it@comma{} after asking if the input holds something else; sending replaces it for everyone (WhatsApp allows edits for about 20 minutes@comma{} and not of attachments);
@item
@samp{d} (@code{wsp-chat-delete}) deletes one of your messages for everyone@comma{} after asking;
@item
@samp{+} (@code{wsp-chat-react}) reacts with an emoji; an empty answer removes your reaction;
@item
@samp{w} (@code{wsp-chat-copy}) copies its text.
@end itemize

@findex wsp-chat-attach-file
@samp{C-c C-a} (@code{wsp-chat-attach-file}) sends a file@comma{} with an optional caption; wa-archive sends images as photos and anything else as a document.  If a reply is in progress@comma{} the file is the reply.

