@end menu

@node What happens when you send
@subsection What happens when you send

@findex wsp-chat-dismiss-pending
Every action (sending@comma{} editing@comma{} deleting@comma{} reacting) goes to wa-archive with an operation id@comma{} and has one of three outcomes:

@itemize
@item
@strong{Done}: the daemon sent it and stored it@comma{} and it appears in the history.  Until then it shows below the history as @samp{sending…}.
@item
@strong{Failed}: nothing went out.  The text returns to the input if the input is empty@comma{} and the echo area says why.
@item
@strong{Uncertain}: the answer was lost@comma{} so it may have gone out.  @samp{wsp} asks the daemon what became of the operation@comma{} again whenever the connection comes back and whenever the store changes@comma{} and settles it as done or failed once the daemon knows.  An answer that arrives late settles it too.  Until then the text stays below the history marked @samp{may have been sent}; once you have checked your phone@comma{} press @samp{x} on it (@code{wsp-chat-dismiss-pending}).  @samp{wsp} never sends anything again on its own@comma{} since a send whose answer was lost may well have arrived.  Killing the buffer forgets such sends@comma{} and the echo area says how many.
@end itemize

A failed message or edit goes back to the input together with what it replied to or edited@comma{} so @samp{RET} retries it as it was.  Sending a file waits up to ten minutes for the upload before its outcome counts as unknown.

If wa-archive cannot be reached@comma{} the action is refused at once and nothing is pending.

@node Attachments
@section Attachments

@findex wsp-chat-open-at-point
Attachments show as a label such as @samp{[image: photo.jpg]} or @samp{[voice message]}.  wa-archive downloads voice notes and audio as they arrive@comma{} and transcribes them; the transcript appears under the label.  Other attachments are downloaded on request.

@samp{RET} or @samp{o} on a message (@code{wsp-chat-open-at-point}) opens what is there: a web or mail link in the browser (other links@comma{} such as @samp{file:} ones@comma{} are refused); an image@comma{} video or document with the system's default application; a voice note or audio with the first of @code{wsp-audio-players}@comma{} or stops it if it is playing.  An attachment not yet downloaded is downloaded first.

@vindex wsp-safe-extensions
Senders name their files@comma{} and the system may run a file rather than show it (a @samp{.terminal} or @samp{.app}@comma{} say).  So only files whose extension is in the user option @code{wsp-safe-extensions} (common images@comma{} video@comma{} audio@comma{} PDF and office documents) open without a question; anything else asks first.  Images appear in the chat once downloaded (@ref{Attachments (1), , Attachments} options).

@node Searching
@section Searching

@findex wsp-search
@findex wsp-search-chat
@findex wsp-search-mode
@findex wsp-search-goto-result
@findex wsp-search-next-result
@findex wsp-search-previous-result
@samp{M-x wsp-search} searches every chat for messages whose text@comma{} latest edit or file name contains the query@comma{} ignoring case; @samp{C-c C-s} in a chat (@code{wsp-search-chat}) searches only that chat.  Deleted messages are not searched.  Results@comma{} newest first@comma{} appear in @samp{*wsp search*}; @samp{n} and @samp{p} move between them and @samp{RET} (@code{wsp-search-goto-result}) opens the chat at the message.

@node Opening a chat at a message
@section Opening a chat at a message

@findex wsp-open-message
@samp{M-x wsp-open-message} opens the chat of a message given its wa-archive reference@comma{} @samp{CHAT_KEY/MSG_ID}@comma{} with point on the message and the message highlighted.  Other programs can record WhatsApp messages by that reference and open them this way.  History is loaded back to the message if needed.  The chat key may be an old alias of the chat@comma{} and if the message has since moved to another chat key@comma{} @samp{wsp} finds it by its id.  A deleted message is still found and shows as @samp{[deleted]}.  If the message is not in the store but its chat is@comma{} the chat opens and the echo area says why; if neither is known@comma{} the command signals an error.  Opening a chat this way marks it read@comma{} like any chat you look at.

@node Read state notifications and the indicator
@section Read state@comma{} notifications and the indicator

A message from someone else is unread until you show its chat in @samp{wsp} (with @code{wsp-mark-read} on) or read it on another device.  Messages archived before wa-archive started keeping read state count as read.  When a chat buffer with unread messages is in the selected window of a focused frame@comma{} @samp{wsp} asks wa-archive to mark them read@comma{} which sends the read receipts.

While @samp{wsp} runs@comma{} each batch of new incoming messages shows one desktop notification per chat@comma{} except for the chat you are looking at.  Only messages that arrived live in the last ten minutes notify@comma{} so history replays and the old messages wa-archive copies when it merges two ids of a chat do not.  If the daemon cannot mark some messages read (for instance in a group you have left)@comma{} @samp{wsp} does not ask again until the chat's unread count changes.  On macOS notifications go through @samp{osascript}@comma{} elsewhere through @samp{notifications.el}.

@findex wsp-indicator-mode
@code{wsp-indicator-mode} is a global minor mode that shows the number of unread messages in the mode line@comma{} as @samp{WA:3}.  It updates while @samp{wsp} runs.

@node The daemon's health
@section The daemon's health

wa-archive writes a heartbeat file while connected and leaves a marker when WhatsApp unlinks it or rejects it as outdated.  @samp{wsp} reads these and@comma{} when something is wrong@comma{} shows a warning in the header line of the list and of chat buffers: unlinked@comma{} outdated@comma{} no heartbeat@comma{} or a heartbeat older than @code{wsp-heartbeat-max-age}.  Then recent messages may be missing.  A chat buffer also says when @samp{wsp} is not connected to the daemon@comma{} in which case it can read but not act.

