@node Opening a message from another package
@section Opening a message from another package

@findex wsp-message-buffer
@code{wsp-message-buffer} takes a reference @samp{CHAT_KEY/MSG_ID} and returns the chat buffer with point on the message@comma{} without changing any window.  It is for programs that show the message in a window of their own choosing@comma{} such as a split view next to a list of messages.  When the message is not in the store it signals @code{wsp-message-not-found}@comma{} a kind of @code{user-error}@comma{} whose data is @samp{(REASON CHAT-BUFFER)}: CHAT-BUFFER is the chat's buffer when the chat is known@comma{} else @code{nil}.

@lisp
(condition-case err
    (set-window-buffer window (wsp-message-buffer ref))
  (wsp-message-not-found
   (when-let* ((chat (nth 2 err)))
     (set-window-buffer window chat))
   (message "%s" (nth 1 err))))
@end lisp

@node Building blocks
@section Building blocks

@findex wsp-start
@findex wsp-chat-buffer
@findex wsp-chat-open
@findex wsp-chat-show-message
@findex wsp-api-request
@findex wsp-db-chats
@findex wsp-db-messages
@findex wsp-db-message
@code{wsp-start} connects to wa-archive and starts redrawing; every command calls it.  @code{wsp-chat-buffer} returns a chat's buffer@comma{} creating it if needed@comma{} and @code{wsp-chat-open} also displays it; both take a chat key or an alias of one.  In a chat buffer@comma{} @code{wsp-chat-show-message} loads history back to a message id and puts point on it.

@code{wsp-api-request} sends a request to the daemon and calls a callback with its result and error; the methods are those of wa-archive's API@comma{} described in @samp{docs/api.md} in the repository.  @code{wsp-db-chats}@comma{} @code{wsp-db-messages} and @code{wsp-db-message} read chats and messages from the store as plists.

